  "term": "lisdexamfetamine",
  "definition": "Lisdexamfetamine is a stimulant-related drug that is inactive until the body converts it to dextroamphetamine. The active form increases central nervous system activity by boosting noradrenaline and dopamine signaling, which can change behavior and alertness and may suppress appetite.",
